<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak November key M2 money up 19.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Slovak November key M2 money up 19.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said on Wednesday its key money supply measure, M2, rose 19.0 percent year-on-year in November, compared with a 17.9 percent increase in October.  </p>
<p> SLOVAK MONEY SUPPLY   Nov'96   Oct'96   Sept'96   Nov'95</p>
<p>M2 overall</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	+19.0    +17.9     +19.0	n/a</p>
<p>pct change</p>
<p>  as of Jan 1	     +8.4     +5.3	+5.8    +10.7</p>
<p>Note. M2 measures currency, demand and time deposits, savings deposits, and foreign currency deposits.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-563-3687</p>
